title: Proposition 22
---
order: 22
---
short_label: III.22
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The sum of the opposite angles of quadrilaterals in circles equals two right angles.
----
proof:

Let *ABCD* be a circle, and let *ABCD* be a quadrilateral in it.

I say that the sum of the opposite angles equals two right angles.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="260" height="230" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.22 diagram" src="propIII22.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "III.22",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,50",
            "B;point;free;200,40",
            "C;point;free;200,180",
            "ABCD;circle;circumcircle;A,B,C;0;0;0,0,0;random",
            "D;point;circleSlider;ABCD,120,200",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Join *AC* and *BD.*

Then, since in any triangle the sum of the three angles equals two right angles, the sum of the three angles *CAB, ABC,* and *BCA* of the triangle *ABC* equals two right angles. [!just I.32]

But the angle *CAB* equals the angle *BDC,* for they are in the same segment *BADC,* and the angle *ACB* equals the angle *ADB,* for they are in the same segment *ADCB,* therefore the whole angle *ADC* equals the sum of the angles *BAC* and *ACB.* [!just III.21]

Add the angle *ABC* to each. Therefore the sum of the angles *ABC, BAC,* and *ACB* equals the sum of the angles *ABC* and *ADC.*  But the sum of the angles *ABC, BAC,* and *ACB* equals two right angles, therefore the sum of the angles *ABC* and *ADC* also equal two right angles.

Similarly we can prove that the sum of the angles *BAD* and *DCB* also equals two right angles.

Therefore *the sum of the opposite angles of quadrilaterals in circles equals two right angles.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is used in @III.31 and @III.32.
